* ''One root branch, `develop`'' (operator, 2026-11-07: //"So MU the workspace question."// and, truing it, //"the primary repo here will just serve `develop` until the roadmap clears, no split needed, we dogfood and develop on one checked out root-nbrach `develop`, then PR back to main after milestones."//). PR #218 carried the span to `main` (`e844e0d8b`, 2026-11-17), and `develop` stands cut from it at the same commit: the main repo checks out one root branch, `develop`, where the house both dogfoods and develops until the roadmap clears; lanes branch off `develop` and land into it, the live wiki's writes land there as source-control write-back, and `main` carries releases (operator, 2026-11-17: //"Now spirits and changes can get working branches merged into a living `develop` and we can plan 'releases' from main in full CICD modern software fashion!"//), each planned and cut by a pull request from `develop`, the release plan owed at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/develop-flow.

